HyperMOS LOCK seed mode (hybrid) — marker file, existence is the switch.

When this file is present, bin/package/TNM/patch.sh calls
integrate_lock.py --helper-only: the ROM installs system_ext/xbin/tnm_helper
plus its SELinux policy, file_contexts and fs_config rows, and deletes the
vendor/odm precompiled_sepolicy caches, but does NOT append the managed
`on post-fs` block to system/etc/init/hw/init.rc.

The post-fs trigger then comes from the SukiSU/KernelSU root module
(hypermos_lock v1.1.0-hybrid, initrc/hypermos_lock.rc), not from the ROM.
Toggling LOCK after the seed ROM is flashed is therefore a module
enable/disable in the manager, with no ROM rebuild.

Deleting this file restores the original full-LOCK behaviour on the next
build (ROM init.rc block included). Do not delete it while the hybrid
module is the intended trigger, or the ROM and module blocks will run
twice with the same values (harmless but redundant).
